# ============================================================================
# CINDERWICK CITY  (ironworks city, 26x22 blocks, buffer 896/1300) johto_modern
# ============================================================================
# HOOK: a soot-and-brick factory city split by the railed Cinder Canal. North
#   of the water stands the fenced Cinderwick Ironworks, whose Furnace Tower
#   and its stack are the tallest things for miles; south of it is the
#   lively downtown. The furnace has gone cold: wild Slugma/Magby (and a
#   Koffing infestation) have nested in the flue, the works is locked, and
#   the Gym leader -- BRENNA, head smelter, FIRE-type -- is inside trying to
#   relight it. The Gym stays shut until you help clear the Furnace Tower.
#
# DISTRICTS / BUILDINGS (door steps are the exit lines below)
#   The Rows (NW, rows 1-8): four terraces of workers' cottages, 5 doors
#     open (rest are shut fronts). Workers' Hall (3x2) = union hall: a
#     shift-board NPC trades/tutors, foreman's notice about the cold furnace.
#     Small flower garden under the Hall; street trees (2f) on the avenue.
#   Cinderwick Ironworks (NE, fenced compound rows 1-8; gate = gap in the
#     west fence on row 4, guarded until the story opens it)
#     Furnace Tower (2x3 tower + 3-block stack, radio-tower art) - landmark
#       and a 3-4 floor dungeon: Worker/Engineer trainers, Slugma/Magby/
#       Koffing, Brenna on the top floor; relighting it opens the Gym
#     Warehouse A (brown roof, 2x2 + sealed bay) - ore store, items
#     Warehouse B (brown roof) - foreman's office; gives a Charcoal/Fire item
#     Slag heaps (0a) between the warehouses; hidden item in them
#   Cinder Canal (rows 9-10): railed canal end to end, bridges at cols 4-5
#     and on the avenue; flows off W and E (a Surf link to the next maps)
#   Canal Street (row 11): brick embankment, west exit.
#   Downtown (SW): Furnace Hotel (3x4 tower; lobby PC + paid rest, NO
#     Pokemon Center), Mart, Mart plaza (planter, plaza sign), Market Row
#     (five stall kiosks on brick with merchants in front), three houses.
#   Station Square (SE): fenced Cooling Pond (decorative; hidden item by its
#     east fence), Freight Station (3x2, door on its west end) - cargo line /
#     magnet-train freight to Goldenrod, Gym (4x2) on a brick forecourt,
#     one house; East Road leaves on row 15.
#
# GAMEPLAY BEATS
#   1. Arrive from the west on Canal Street (or north/south on the avenue).
#   2. Gym trainee at the door: "Brenna's at the works, the furnace died."
#   3. Workers' Hall foreman hands you a works pass; gate guard steps aside.
#   4. Furnace Tower dungeon; Brenna relights the furnace (at night the
#      tower windows glow -- see the _nite render), Gym opens.
#   5. Gym battle. Post-Surf: canal ends W/E, hidden items on canal banks.
#
# EXITS / CONNECTIONS
#   N  avenue cols 12-13 (steps 24-25)  -> a route north
#   S  avenue cols 12-13               -> a route south
#   W  Canal Street row 11 (step y 22-23); canal water rows 9-10 also exit W
#   E  East Road row 15 (step y 30-31);   canal water rows 9-10 also exit E
# NOTE: block 1d is the GYM-labelled front; used only on the Gym (1c 0f 1d 1e).
# TILE GAPS / UNCERTAIN
#   - No chimney/smokestack block: the stack is the Radio Tower mast (21 22
#     22) above the 25/26 tower body; it reads as a tall stack but carries a
#     dish on top. A dedicated stack or smoke tile would sell it.
#   - No rail-track or crane block for a freight yard; 7e/7f are fence/ledge.
#   - Gate is a plain gap in the 44 fence side (no gatepost graphic).
#   - Cooling Pond top edge is 35 water under a 41 fence, as in Silkwater.
#   - Warehouses reuse 08/09 brown roofs over 16 1e / 2b 2c (Brinehaven).
# ============================================================================
tileset johto_modern
ref GoldenrodCity
key T=05 .=01 :=06 ,=02 *=04 h=67 o=0a ~=35 n=43 u=61
key <=44 >=46 r=40 f=41 t=42 l=48 e=49 j=4a s=45 S=77 w=66 x=80 z=81
